[[File:Collection log detail.png|left|130px]]
The '''collection log''' is a [[book]] that players can receive from [[The Collector]] near the stairs in the [[Varrock Museum]]'s {{FloorNumber|uk=0}}. It records nearly every unique drop the player has obtained from various content in ''[[Old School RuneScape]]''. The player does not need to have claimed a collection log for it to start tracking drops.

Drops obtained prior to its release are not automatically recorded for any player, excluding untradeable items (such as [[pet]]s) provided that they can be tracked by the game; for example, [[long bone]]s the player had traded to [[Barlak]] or buried before the log's release were not added to it, but any long bones in the player's possession were added. [[Ironman Mode|Ironman]] players are able to add some items collected prior to the release by using the item on the collection log item; this does not apply to [[Group Ironman Mode|Group Ironman]] players. Using an ineligible or already logged item on the collection log gives the message {{mes|Your collection log has already accounted for that item.}}

Each entry in the log is tracked by the item itself, not where it was obtained. This means that collection log item slots can be shared across multiple pages. For example, obtaining a [[dragon pickaxe]] from the [[Chaos Elemental]] will also log it under other bosses that drop it, such as [[Callisto]] and the [[King Black Dragon]].

There is a cap on the amount each item can be tracked, depending on the item in question. For example, [[Zulrah's scales]] will only be tracked up to 65,535 and [[Bracelet of ethereum|bracelets of ethereum]] up to 250.

It can be stored in a [[bookcase]] within a [[player-owned house]], and can also be accessed from the adventurer's log within a player's [[Achievement Gallery]] and the [[Character Summary]] interface.

There are currently a total of 1,906 slots to fill in the collection log, with a total of {{formatnum:{{Globals|collection log slots}}}} unique entries being tracked. Pets, [[gilded equipment]], and [[3rd age equipment]] account for 126 of the 201 slots containing duplicate items.

